  "Every New York clip nyc.daily.aesthetic may use, looked at by eye (2026-11-24) and labelled from the picture, not",
  "from the stock title (Pexels called the Manhattan Bridge the Brooklyn Bridge). Keyed by the library asset.",
  "place/area: the label shown on the cut (only where the picture shows it). ll: the landmark's coordinates (Wikipedia).",
  "mood: day, sunset, night, snow (picks the hook line). hero 0-3: how well it opens a video (3 = a frame worth stopping for).",
  "pair: the same place in old film and today, for the then-and-now split. year: when an old film was made (from the index).",
  "skip: never used, and why. A clip of theme nyc_now or nyc not listed here is used with no label and hero 0.",
  "For old films hero picks the opening film too (the bright shots of the bridge towers, not the dark truss).",
  "Pairs are kept only where both halves show the same place (the bridge, the river): the 1905 subway and the 1905 rooftops had no honest match today.",
  "tags: what is in the picture, looked at 2026-11-27 (fire escape, snow, night, window view, park, river, look up,",
  "bridge, street sign, empty street, traffic, taxi, train, sunset, rooftops, sidewalk, slush, steam ...). A meme line in",
  "studio/nyc/memes.txt opens on a clip whose tags hold its needs: tag; a line no clip has waits until one does."
 ],
